:: StoryTitle
The Ninefold Cell: the duel, step 2 (typed fields)

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.6.0",
  "start": "sanctum"
}

:: Inklink [config]
(((
Step 2 of `define` (docs/define.md): an archetype may declare fields, typed
and checked, which things `like` it fill in and anything may read as
`x.field`. Builds on step 1 (`ex2-duel-step1-like.twee`); only what differs
from it is here.

What step 2 adds:

| Word | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `field school: fire, frost, sound, time` | One of these words; `~ school fier` is an error |
| `field hit: text ~ default ""` | Text, with braces and emphasis like any quoted text |
| `field power: number`, `duration`, a kind | Not needed by the duel |

Two places in the duel can use fields: the school of a spell (the tags
`fire`, `frost` and `loud` in steps 0 and 1), and the Host's lines for each
outcome of each threat, which the general draft keeps in `[resolve]`.
)))

item abelard_sword: "Abelard’s longsword" ~ like sword ~ deflects school fire ~ in well

:: spell [archetype]
verb: cast
for: roland
field school: fire, frost, sound, time
--

:: hex [archetype]
verb: casts
field school: fire, frost, light, none ~ default none
field hit: text ~ default ""
field block: text ~ default ""
field deflect: text ~ default ""
field fail: text ~ default ""
--

:: roland [character]
state rewound: no
--
combo ember_lance: spark, gust, spark ~ like spell ~ school fire ~ "flame, fanned, then lit into a lance"
~ at character here ~ when target.frozen
~ then set target.frozen: no
combo rime_shield: chill, mend, chill ~ like spell ~ school frost ~ "a shell of ice that heals its own cracks"
~ at character here
~ then cover target
combo frostglass: chill, gust ~ like spell ~ school frost ~ "rimes a mirror over until it shows nothing"
~ at mirror here ~ when target.open
~ then set target.open: no
combo thunderclap: hush, gust, spark ~ like spell ~ school sound ~ loud ~ "a swallowed sound, carried, then let go at once"
~ then prevent hask when hask.rhyme.next.school in [fire, frost]
combo backward_knot: mend, hush, tug, mend ~ like spell ~ school time ~ "ties the hour back on itself"
~ rewind ~ once per turn ~ requires pov.all alive

act lodestone: cost 30 ~ like spell ~ school time ~ learned from lodestone ~ when roland.knows.lodestone
~ "makes one thing very, very heavy, for one breath"
~ at npc here
~ then set target.grounded: yes
~ then pin target

:: hask_duel [npc]
--
stat wards: 3
stat wards: 2 when heart.cracked

pattern rhyme: flame, frost, blink, sunfall ~ repeat ~ one per round
~ recall first when hask.saw_heart and holder != nobody and not heart.cracked
~ falter instead of sunfall when holder != nobody and not heart.cracked

threat flame ~ like hex ~ school fire ~ at roland ~ answered by prevent, block, cover, absorb
~ then wound target 1
~ hit "Fire takes Roland full in the chest."
~ block "Eldric takes the fire meant for Roland on his own chest, and staggers, and stays up."
~ deflect "Eldric turns the flame aside on Abelard’s blade, and it splashes harmless across the floor."
threat frost ~ like hex ~ school frost ~ at eldric ~ answered by prevent, cover, absorb
~ then kill target when target.frozen
~ then set target.frozen: yes
~ hit "Ice climbs Eldric to the shoulders and holds him fast."
threat blink ~ like hex ~ fails when count(mirror, in: here, open: yes) == 0 or hask.pinned
~ then set hask.dodging: yes
~ then set hask.grounded: yes next round
~ on fail: set hask.grounded: yes
~ hit "He steps into a mirror and out of the other, and lands on his feet, laughing."
~ fail "He throws himself at the glass and hits frost, hard. He lands on the flagstones in a heap of robes."
threat sunfall ~ like hex ~ school light ~ at pov.all ~ answered by cover, absorb
~ then kill target
~ hit "Light, all of it, everywhere at once."
threat recall ~ like hex ~ at holder ~ answered by block, cover, absorb
~ then take heart
~ hit "The heart leaps from your hand to his, like a dog called home."
threat falter ~ like hex
~ hit "Nothing. He will not burn his own heart, and he knows you know it."

:: sanctum:spell [resolve]
--
[if threat.outcome == hit]
{threat.hit}

[if threat.outcome == block]
{threat.block}

[if threat.outcome == deflect]
{threat.deflect}

[if threat.outcome == fail]
{threat.fail}

[if threat.outcome == cover]
The spell breaks on {threat.target}’s ice and runs off it like rain off a window.

[if threat.outcome == absorb]
Lumen drinks the spell whole and begins to glow.

[if threat.outcome == prevent]
Nothing comes. The spell died in his hands.

[end]
> [[Next round->sanctum:round]] ~ when hask.wards > 0 and pov.any.up
> [[He falls->fallen]] ~ when hask.wards == 0
